**How to implement.** The composition root reads every location from `appsettings.json` through the settings doors, and the test run pins its own (001 §G 'Every path is overridable'; 001 §C 'Settings': the connection string is the `OpticalConstructorSqlite` entry; .spec-md §3.9). (1) `OpticalConstructor.App/AppConfig.fs`. (a) Module `ConfigKey` (`AppConfig.fs:22`) gains six appSettings literals, each with a one-line doc naming its `DataLocations` field: `libraryBackupsFolder` = `"LibraryBackupsFolder"`, `preferencesFolder` = `"PreferencesFolder"`, `kitsFolder` = `"KitsFolder"`, `exportsFolder` = `"ExportsFolder"`, `cataloguesFolder` = `"CataloguesFolder"` and `shippedCatalogueFolder` = `"ShippedCatalogueFolder"`. `sqliteConnectionString` (`"OpticalConstructorSqlite"`, the connectionStrings entry) is the library connection and keeps its name. (b) Module `AppConfig` gains `readDataLocations (provider : AppSettings.AppSettingsProvider) (install : FolderName) (documents : FolderName) : DataLocations`, documented in one to three lines: each location is read once, a missing or refused one is written back as its default (`DataLocations.defaultsUnder documents`, step 81), and the answer has environment variables expanded and a relative folder rooted at `install`. It works in this order. The connection string is `provider.tryGetConnectionString` on `ConfigKey.sqliteConnectionString`: `Ok (Some value)` is kept; `Ok None` and `Error _` write the default back through `provider.trySetConnectionString` and use it, and an `Error` of the read or of the write-back is named in a `Logger.logWarn`, as `readSetting` (`AppConfig.fs:117`) names a refused value. Each folder is `readSetting provider (AppSettings.ConfigKey ConfigKey.<key>) defaults.<field> FolderName.tryCreate _.configValue`, STL's `FolderName` door (`Softellect.Sys.AppSettings`), so a missing or refused folder is logged and its default written back exactly as today's four keys are. The configured texts, gathered as a `DataLocations`, are then resolved by the private `resolveLocations (install : FolderName) (configured : DataLocations) : DataLocations`: `System.Environment.ExpandEnvironmentVariables` over the connection string and over each folder, and a folder that is not rooted after expansion (`Path.IsPathRooted`) combined under `install`. Each value is elevated where it is born (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). This is the IO boundary; Domain reads no environment. It does not save: its caller saves once, as `loadWorkbenchSettings` does today. `loadWorkbenchSettings` (`AppConfig.fs:136`) and its callers are unchanged in this step; step 83 makes it read the locations. (2) The test run's settings. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/appsettings.json`, a `Content` item of `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` with `CopyToOutputDirectory` `PreserveNewest` and no comment. A project's own copy item wins over a referenced project's item of the same target path (MSBuild removes the transitive item by `TargetPath`), so it replaces the App's `appsettings.json` (`OpticalConstructor.App.fsproj` `Content`) in the test output. That file is what the headless session's real `App` startup reads (`TestApp.fs:31-35`, `Program.fs:48`, `SmokeTests`), and from step 88 that startup opens the configured library. It holds `connectionStrings.OpticalConstructorSqlite` = `Data Source=:memory:` and, in `appSettings`, `LibraryBackupsFolder` = `TestRun/Backups`, `PreferencesFolder` = `TestRun/Preferences`, `KitsFolder` = `TestRun/Kits`, `ExportsFolder` = `TestRun/Exports`, `CataloguesFolder` = `TestRun/Catalogues` and `ShippedCatalogueFolder` = `Catalogue`: relative folders, so each resolves under the test output, and the build-copied catalogue. No test run therefore reaches `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, `%APPDATA%` or `Documents` (.spec-md §3.9, §4 "Tests' data"). (3) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/AppConfigTests.fs`, `module AppConfigTests`, compiled directly after `LauncherTests.fs`. Every settings file of (a)-(c) is `appsettings.json` in a fresh folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "AppConfigTests")`, opened through `AppSettings.AppSettingsProvider.tryCreate (FileName <path>)`; `install` and `documents` are folders under that fresh folder; nothing is created at a resolved location. (a) `readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded`: over `{ "appSettings": {}, "connectionStrings": {} }`, the answer's `libraryConnection` is the expansion of the default connection string and each folder the expansion of its default (`shippedCatalogueFolder` being `Catalogue` under `install`); after `trySave` the file holds the default texts verbatim, `%LOCALAPPDATA%` and `%APPDATA%` unexpanded. (b) `readDataLocations keeps a configured location, expands its variables and roots a relative folder at the install folder`: with a process environment variable the fact sets to a folder under its own test folder (a name no other code reads, removed in a `finally`), a configured `Data Source=%<variable>%/lib.db`, a configured `%<variable>%/Backups` and a configured relative `Kits` answer the expanded connection string, the expanded folder and `Kits` under `install`, and the file still holds the configured texts. (c) `readDataLocations replaces a refused folder with its default and writes the default back`: a configured `KitsFolder` that `FolderName.tryCreate` refuses (it holds `|`) answers the default kits folder, and the default is written back over it. (d) `the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output`: inside `HeadlessSession.run`, so the session's `App` startup, the only other writer of that file, has finished, `readDataLocations` over the test output's own `appsettings.json` with `install` = `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` answers `Data Source=:memory:`, five folders under the test output, and `Catalogue` there as the shipped catalogue.

**Acceptance.** After the reader lands, `AppConfig.readDataLocations` MUST read every location through `ConfigKey` and the test output's `appsettings.json` MUST hold the test run's locations; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over AppConfigTests, including `readDataLocations writes every missing location back as its default and answers it expanded`, `readDataLocations keeps a configured location, expands its variables and roots a relative folder at the install folder`, `readDataLocations replaces a refused folder with its default and writes the default back` and `the test run's appsettings.json keeps the library in memory and every folder under the test output`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.
